Z||000000||fropuff||11-04-2000||07:15 PM||||Hey, I know I'm annoying everyone with my retarded speaker questions, but I can't help it.  I was wondering if I could get some other speakers to put in the 4x10 space on the dash.  I wanted to do 6x9s, but I don't really want to cut or remove the dash.  What others would work, other than the 4x10?  Does anyone have any pictures of them?  I've heard round speakers are better than oval.  Does anyone have 5 1/4s in their dash?    WTIII, do you have any pictures of your setup?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||5
Z||000001||BroCar 87||11-04-2000||07:21 PM||||Hey Fropuff, I believe two 4" speakers in each hole(4 total speakers in dash) would sound best! That is the set up I plan on doing. Just a suggestion for ya  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||6
Z||000002||fropuff||11-04-2000||07:58 PM||||That sounds like a great idea!  I never really thought of four of them though; just two, but four would sound great!  4" sell fro pretty cheap at Best Buy too.  I'm glad I didn't get my 6x9s today.  With this 4-4" thing, I suppose I could come up with a type of plate to accept them.  Good idea.  Thanks!  Anyone have a problem with it?  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||11-04-2000||08:14 PM||||I may be wrong, but just thinking it over in my head, it sounds like you would have to remove the dash to do it. I think you may be able to get away with top mounting one 4" on each side, but 2 on each side might be pushing it. Just make a wooden plate with the cut out dia. of the speaker in the middle. I put 4" Polk Ex components in my dash, one on each side, but I removed the dash and sealed a plate to the bottem of the dash for sound quality. Useing some rubber speaker baffels will help also.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">   <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||11-04-2000||08:20 PM||||That's kind of what I was planning on.  I will have to see though.  I just didn't want to have to remove the dash, but I will if I get some good sound from them.  I just didn't look forward to it, but I can do a little each day, starting tomorrow when I get them.  All car speakers are on sale this week!  Seanh, how do your 4s sound in the front?  Will I have to do any special wiring, other than having to cut the harness off and wiring directly?  Thanks a lot.  I might actually stick with this idea.  I think I can somewhat afford it too.  Thanks again.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||10
Z||000005||Oreif||11-04-2000||09:02 PM||||I made a 4X10 plate out of wood and mounted a set of Polk Audio 4" ES speakers in the middle and the tweeter is mouted towards the outside edge. The foam baffle behind helps the mid-bass of the speaker. I am putting 4X6 Infinity Kappa plates (3 1/2" with seperate tweeter) in the sail panels and an 8" sub behind the passenger seat.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||11-04-2000||09:05 PM||||i  would think you could get 2 4s in each side. probaly with a tweeter also. or possibly a 4x6 plate (that has a 3.5 or 4 with a tweeter) with an added 4" woofer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||11-04-2000||11:25 PM||||If you use a component setup, like mine, and will most midranges, you have to run the existing speaker wires into a crossover (comes with the speaker kit), and then run 2 sets of speaker wires out, one set to the midrange, and one set to the tweeter. I think 4" midranges are the best possible design for a stereo system in the Fiero. Notice I said system. If you are not planning on putting a large sub (8" or up) in, then your not going to get much bass from the stereo. 4" mids are designed to put out the freq. a little higher then the sub freq. If you go with just regular 4" speakers, I dont know what kind of result your going to get. I install stereo systems here, and we always use component systems. You will get your best performance out of a round speaker. With the exception of the Kicker square subs, I like those. I would recomend, for a limited budget to do the following: Put a set (or two) 4" midrange component set up front. Throw in some Pioneer or Infinity Knappa 4x6 plates (round woofer and tweeter, not oval speaker) in the rear, and either an 8" in the stock location or footwell, or 10" up front ported into the cabin. With a little time this can be built yourself, if you dont mind loosing the spare tire, jack, and cutting off the bottem of the spare tire pod up front. Also, no matter what, for good performance the sub should be amped. With a good headunit you should be able to get good sound from the 4 speakers in the stock locations.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">    <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I><p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 11-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||11-05-2000||12:36 AM||||  Fropuff, check out this site, it belongs to a Forum member. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/</A>   You will like what he has done. I plan on doing some of these things but would never completely plagiarize the setup. It's AWESOME!!!!!<P><BR>  Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||10
